What:           /sys/class/power_supply/oplus-pmic-pps/curve
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Yibo Wang <wyibo6109@gmail.com>
Description:
                Write-only transactional PPS curve replacement. First write 1
                to the standard online attribute to restore basic charging and
                disable automatic PPS. From one process, write "begin 1", then
                one row per write, then "commit" (or "abort"). Each row contains
                ten decimal integers: SOC lower/upper percent (inclusive),
                temperature lower/upper deci-Celsius (half-open), gear, source
                mV, battery threshold mV, source mA, flags, timeout seconds.
                Flags: 1 = last gear, 2 = CV. Format and validation match DT.
                A failed transaction leaves the previous table untouched;
                abort or begin a new transaction to recover. After committing,
                write 2 to online to enable automatic PPS again. The original
                DT table is loaded afresh on probe; reloads are not persistent.

What:           /sys/class/power_supply/oplus-pmic-pps/policy_state
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Yibo Wang <wyibo6109@gmail.com>
Description:
                Read-only policy state (basic/running/suspended/fault), last
                error and requested mV/mA. A requested target is not a VBUS
                measurement. Standard voltage_now/current_now report the last
                PMIC measurements collected by policy work, in uV/uA.
                ONLINE=0 means disconnected, 1 basic, 2 PPS. Writing online=1
                restores basic charging, not charge inhibition; online=2
                enables automatic PPS. PPS stops on an invalid measurement,
                curve exhaustion or communication failure. Faults are latched
                until unplug or an explicit online write. When block_suspend=0,
                suspend restores basic charging before device suspend, then
                resumes event-driven PPS on PM_POST_SUSPEND. No userspace
                daemon is required.

What:           /sys/class/power_supply/oplus-pmic-pps/block_suspend
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Yibo Wang <wyibo6109@gmail.com>
Description:
                Read/write boolean, default 1 on every probe. While enabled,
                USB power online holds a native wakeup source, including basic
                charging and a fully charged battery. This keeps the policy
                running without interrupting PPS for system sleep. USB removal
                releases the hold. System suspend/hibernation preparation also
                rechecks the connection and returns -EBUSY while online, without
                changing the active charging policy. If the connection cannot
                be read, preparation fails with that error rather than risking
                a charging interruption.

                Write 0 to release the hold and allow normal system sleep;
                the driver must still restore basic charging before sleeping.
                Write 1 to enable the policy again. This preference is separate
                from the standard online property and does not enable/disable
                PPS or charging. Writes during sleep preparation or teardown
                return -EBUSY. The value is not persistent across reprobe.
